# Project structure (iOS app under `ios/Vuum/`)

Keep code in its existing module. Do **not** create parallel/duplicate files.
Search before adding a new file.

## Folder map

- `App/` — entry + splash gate + `RootFlowView` phase router
- `Models/` — trip / place / driver / tier types
- `Services/` — `TripSession` (demo state machine only)
- `Mock/` — sample places, drivers, fares
- `Maps/` — Google Maps bootstrap + `VuumMapView`
- `UI/Theme/` — `VuumColor`, `VuumTheme` (ComponentsKit accent bootstrap)
- `UI/Components/` — glass surfaces, chrome, UIKit bridges
- `UI/Flow/` — rider-flow screens (scaffold → polish)
- `reference/` — docs for ComponentsKit + Explore SwiftUI (not product screens)

## Do NOT

- Copy screens or branding from `Wells-Gas-Level-Monitor-main/`
- Put trip logic in SwiftUI views — keep it in `TripSession`
- Commit real Google Maps API keys
- Reintroduce Firebase / BLE unless product scope changes

## Packages (SPM)

- ComponentsKit — `https://github.com/componentskit/ComponentsKit`
- GoogleMaps — `https://github.com/googlemaps/ios-maps-sdk`

SwiftUI + UIKit are system frameworks (always available).

## Adding files to the build

Classic Xcode project: register new `.swift` files in
`ios/Vuum.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj` (PBXFileReference + PBXBuildFile + group + Sources).
